fact WorkItem(id: "WI-563", description: some(value: "anthill-smt-gen v0: handle uninterpreted-function body goals. After WI-562 unblocked the lf1 load, discharge.sh reports 4 failing proofs: safety_max_distance, safety_min_distance, safety_no_collision_transponder, safety_bounded_excursion_transponder — all 'v0: unhandled body goal functor position_distance' (anthill-smt-gen/src/lib.rs:616). position_distance is documented (safety_gps.anthill:276) as an UNINTERPRETED free function symbol; the smt-gen body-goal translator has no path for a functor with no ground facts and no defining body — it should emit a Z3 (declare-fun position_distance ...) and assert the goal as an uninterpreted relation. These 4 proofs were ADDED AFTER WI-100 (Apr 28, when discharge.sh reported 7 proved) and were NEVER validated because discharge.sh had been broken by the WI-562 regression since 2026-05-29 — so they are pre-existing-unvalidated, not a WI-562 regression. Acceptance: discharge.sh reports all proofs proved (currently 10 proved, 4 failed); add an smt-gen test for an uninterpreted-relation body goal. See also the spec's documented predicate-status table in safety_common.anthill."), context: none, acceptance: [ToolPasses(tool: "cargo-test", params: none)], depends_on: some(value: nil), generates: none, requires_capability: none, status: Delivered(agent: "claude", at: "2026-06-25T06:23:33Z"))

fact Tag(workitem: "WI-563", name: "prop025_1")

fact Feedback(workitem: "WI-563", author: "user", content: "Diagnosis corrected during implementation (user-confirmed). The 4 proofs did NOT fail because position_distance is uninterpreted — it HAS a defining rule body (safety_common.anthill:264, added after the predicate-status table was written). They failed because position_distance was not IMPORTED in safety_gps/safety_transponder, so the functor never resolved to the qualified ...common symbol and try_inline_rule_call returned false → loud 'unhandled body goal functor' error (the short name in the error was the tell). These pointwise refutation proofs REQUIRE inlining position_distance to the concrete initial geometry (?d=4.0) for lt(?d,d_min=1.0) to be unsat; the WI's prescribed declare-fun/uninterpreted-relation path would leave ?d free → spurious SAT → still failing, AND would be a bug-masking silent fallback contrary to the repo 'loud error over silent skip' principle. Fix delivered: (1) import position_distance in safety_gps + safety_transponder; (2) corrected the stale predicate-status table (line 502: 'UNINTERPRETED/No rule body' → DEFINED+UNFOLDED-by-pointwise-proofs) and the inductive-proof note at safety_gps:276 that misled the WI author; (3) new smt-gen test cross_namespace_inline_test.rs guarding cross-namespace inline-to-unsat AND that an unresolved functor stays a loud error (no silent uninterpreted fallback) — this replaces the WI's 'uninterpreted-relation body goal' test, which would have encoded the wrong behavior. discharge.sh now 14 proved / 0 failed; full anthill-smt-gen suite green.", at: "2026-06-25T06:23:28Z")
